  "title": "India's Green Energy Transition and Storage Expansion",
  "summary": "The Indian government has approved a ₹14,500 crore funding scheme to establish grid-scale energy storage capacity, covering 92 GWh of storage across three technologies. This initiative aims to support India's renewable energy goals and align with the 2030 target.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The government cleared ₹14,500 crore for grid-scale energy storage between FY27 and FY31.",
      "confidence": 0.95
